  "worked_solution": "Splitting up the difference and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}(6{z}^{2}-5{z}^{4})\\,\\text{d}z & =6{\\int }_{-2}^{1}{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z-5{\\int }_{-2}^{1}{z}^{4}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}\\,{|}_{-2}^{1}-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{z}^{5}\\,{|}_{-2}^{1} \\\\  & =2{z}^{3}\\,{|}_{-2}^{1}-{z}^{5}\\,{|}_{-2}^{1} \\\\  & =2({1}^{3}-(-2)^{3})-({1}^{5}-(-2)^{5}) \\\\  & =2(1+8)-(1+32) \\\\  & =18-33 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
